  dishID: west_lake_fish
  englishName: West Lake Vinegar Fish
  chineseName: 西湖醋鱼
  pinyinName: Xihu Cuyu
  category: 1
  difficulty: 1
  briefDescription: Grass carp poached in water and covered with a sweet and sour vinegar sauce.
  detailedDescription: A traditional dish of Hangzhou cuisine. The fish is cooked to be extremely tender, and the sweet and sour sauce brings out the freshness of the fish without any earthy taste.
  historicalOrigin: Associated with a legend of two brothers in the Song Dynasty.
  culturalSymbolism: Represents righteous anger and brotherhood (from the legend).
  regionalSignificance: Named after the famous West Lake in Hangzhou.
  craftmanshipNotes: Poaching time must be precise to ensure the texture is like crab meat.
  estimatedDuration: 300
  cookingSteps:
  - stepNumber: 1
    title: Prepare Fish
    narrationAudio: {fileID: 0}
    subtitles: Clean the grass carp and cut it into two halves, keeping them connected at the tail.
    narrationDuration: 30
    requiredGesture: 1
    successThreshold: 0.7
    visualGuideAnimation: {fileID: 0}
  completionMessage: The taste of West Lake history in every bite.
